### Create LangGraph Workflow with StateGraph and InMemorySaver in Python

Source: https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/blob/main/docs/docs/tutorials/chatbots/information-gather-prompting.ipynb

Constructs a complete LangGraph workflow with state management, nodes for info gathering and prompt generation, and a tool message handler. Uses InMemorySaver for conversation persistence and defines conditional edges based on state logic. The graph includes START and END nodes with proper edge connections for chatbot flow control.

```python
from langgraph.checkpoint.memory import InMemorySaver
from langgraph.graph import StateGraph, START
from langgraph.graph.message import add_messages
from typing import Annotated
from typing_extensions import TypedDict


class State(TypedDict):
    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]


memory = InMemorySaver()
workflow = StateGraph(State)
workflow.add_node("info", info_chain)
workflow.add_node("prompt", prompt_gen_chain)


@workflow.add_node
def add_tool_message(state: State):
    return {
        "messages": [
            ToolMessage(
                content="Prompt generated!",
                tool_call_id=state["messages"][-1].tool_calls[0]["id"],
            )
        ]
    }


workflow.add_conditional_edges("info", get_state, ["add_tool_message", "info", END])
workflow.add_edge("add_tool_message", "prompt")
workflow.add_edge("prompt", END)
workflow.add_edge(START, "info")
graph = workflow.compile(checkpointer=memory)
```

