### Define, Visualize, and Invoke LangGraph State Machine (TypeScript)

Source: https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/blob/main/docs/docs/tutorials/workflows.md

This snippet demonstrates configuring edges for a LangGraph state machine workflow using `addConditionalEdges` for branching logic and `addEdge` for sequential steps. It then shows how to compile the workflow, generate a Mermaid PNG visualization of the graph, and invoke the chain with an input to process a joke generation task, including conditional output logging. Note: 'workflow' and 'END' are assumed to be defined elsewhere.

```typescript
workflow
  .addConditionalEdges(
    "generate_joke",
    checkPunchline,
    { "Fail": "improve_joke", "Pass": END }
  )
  .addEdge("improve_joke", "polish_joke")
  .addEdge("polish_joke", END);

