### Define Graph State and Build LangGraph Workflow

Source: https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/blob/main/docs/docs/tutorials/reflexion/reflexion.ipynb

This code defines the `State` for the `langgraph` workflow using `TypedDict` and `Annotated` for managing messages. It initializes a `StateGraph` builder with this state and adds nodes for "draft", "execute_tools", and "revise". It then defines the initial edges, connecting "draft" to "execute_tools" and "execute_tools" to "revise", establishing the basic flow of the agent's operation.

```python
from typing import Literal

from langgraph.graph import END, StateGraph, START
from langgraph.graph.message import add_messages
from typing import Annotated
from typing_extensions import TypedDict


class State(TypedDict):
    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]


MAX_ITERATIONS = 5
